<title>GERMANY: Kohl says mark excess revaluation of 1995 recedes.</title>
<headline>Kohl says mark excess revaluation of 1995 recedes.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor Helmut Kohl said that the excessive revaluation of the mark from the spring of 1995 had receded.</p>
<p>&quot;The excessive revaluation of the mark from the spring of 1995 has receded,&quot; Kohl said in a speech to parliament. He said that one was one of the reasons, along with growing world trade, that he was optimistic the German economy would grow by 2.5 percent in 1997.</p>
</text>
